title: 'Decided: switching is its own request, answered before the redraw.'
pid: 64444c78-8033-42b4-9475-dd8cd198b524
body: |2-
  A save of the clean buffer naming the new choice cannot switch it: the
  buffer's overridesHere carriers were drawn for the old choice and the
  tamper check would refuse them. So the switch is a request that sets
  the view's choice and rerenders it from what the server holds, and the
  answer, naming the view and the new choice, comes before the rerender
  stream, as the skgrepo restriction switch's does. The client records
  the choice only from that answer, so a refusal or a privacy challenge,
  which replaces the answer, leaves the buffer as it was.
